{
  "recommendation": "For a personal checking account, Bluest Account appears to be the best fit based on the available ATM information.",
  "comparison": [
    {
      "account": "Bluest Account",
      "Rho_foreign_ATM_fee": "$0",
      "foreign_ATM_operator_fee_rebate": "Up to $50 per monthly statement cycle",
      "important_note": "Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply; amounts above the $50 monthly rebate cap are your responsibility."
    },
    {
      "account": "World Blue International Checking",
      "Rho_foreign_ATM_fee": "$0",
      "foreign_ATM_operator_fee_rebate": "Up to $100 per calendar month",
      "important_note": "This is presented as a business/international checking account. It has a $50 monthly maintenance fee and requires maintaining at least $10,000."
    }
  ],
  "why": "Although World Blue has the larger ATM-fee rebate, its $50 monthly fee and $10,000 balance requirement could outweigh the extra rebate during a three-month trip. Bluest has no Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee and a $50 monthly third-party-fee rebate; its monthly maintenance fee was not specified in the information available to me.",
  "travel_tip": "At foreign ATMs, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than accepting the ATM's currency conversion. Check the displayed surcharge before confirming each withdrawal.",
  "next_step": "If you mean a personal account, Bluest is the stronger preliminary choice. If you expect more than $50 per month in foreign ATM operator fees or can maintain $10,000 and need a business account, World Blue may be worth considering."
}

