{
  "correction": "Based strictly on ATM costs, World Blue—not Bluest—has the stronger benefit for your withdrawal pattern because its foreign ATM operator-fee rebate cap is $100 per month versus $50 for Bluest.",
  "trip_calculation": {
    "withdrawals": 18,
    "amount_per_withdrawal": "$350",
    "total_withdrawn": "$6,300",
    "months": 3
  },
  "comparison": [
    {
      "account": "Bluest Account",
      "Rho_foreign_ATM_fees": "$0",
      "maximum_operator_fee_rebates_over_3_months": "$150",
      "remaining_operator_fees": "Any eligible foreign ATM operator fees above $50 in a month remain your responsibility."
    },
    {
      "account": "World Blue International Checking",
      "Rho_foreign_ATM_fees": "$0",
      "maximum_operator_fee_rebates_over_3_months": "$300",
      "remaining_operator_fees": "Any eligible foreign ATM operator fees above $100 in a month remain your responsibility."
    }
  ],
  "important_tradeoff": "World Blue has a $50 monthly maintenance fee and requires maintaining at least $10,000. Over three months, that is $150 in maintenance fees, assuming the fee applies. World Blue is described as a business/international checking account, while Bluest appears to be a personal account.",
  "bottom_line": "If you are comparing ATM charges only and can open World Blue, it can reimburse up to $150 more in operator fees over the trip. If you are comparing total account cost, the extra $150 in World Blue rebates exactly offsets its three months of stated maintenance fees at most, before considering the $10,000 balance requirement. Bluest remains the more practical preliminary choice for a personal trip, but I should not have presented it as unambiguously cheapest without knowing the ATM operator surcharge or confirming that World Blue is available to you.",
  "fee_example": "If each foreign ATM charges a $5 operator surcharge, you would incur $90 in operator fees over 18 withdrawals. Bluest could rebate all $90, and World Blue could also rebate all $90; World Blue's additional maintenance fees would then make it more expensive overall.",
  "travel_tip": "Choose to be charged in the local currency, not through the ATM's dynamic currency conversion, and check the surcharge shown before confirming the withdrawal."
}
